.php?search=Neoclassicism%20and%20archaeological%20knowledge","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy","france"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-cf747a928cc4","title":"The Grand Tour and collecting antiquity","lane":"history","start":1750,"end":1830,"approx":true,"note":"Elite educational travel supported markets in antiquities, copies, portraits and views. Distinguish a souvenir veduta from a neutral photographic record.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Grand%20Tour%20and%20collecting%20antiquity","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy","britain"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept"},{"id":"t69-fc22f462458d","title":"Veduta and capriccio","lane":"art","start":1750,"end":1830,"approx":true,"note":"A veduta presents a recognisable view; a capriccio combines or invents architectural motifs. Artists may alter a real view for pictorial purposes.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Veduta%20and%20capriccio","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-38822936c244","title":"Cast iron, wrought iron and steel","lane":"architecture","start":1750,"end":1900,"approx":true,"note":"These iron-based materials differ in manufacture and structural behaviour. Their architectural use cannot be inferred from colour or a modern label alone.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.