ed its treatment of street life and mixed uses.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Urban%20functional%20zoning%20and%20its%20critics","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["shared"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept"},{"id":"t68-18977c914eba","title":"Horse and Rider","lane":"art","start":1930,"end":1980,"approx":true,"note":"Unresolved series reference: the photo does not identify a specific Marini sculpture. Broad subject period only, not an individual work date.","creators":["Marino Marini"],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Horse%20and%20Rider","sourceSheets":[3645],"sourceMapping":"contextual identification","dateType":"period","threads67":["italy"],"setting67":"Cultural / geographical association; see work context","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16","dateQualifier":"Source title / version unresolved","mediaType78":"visual-artwork","museumAssetId78":"M77-MOMA-81477","image":{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=5e3f2b5eca9e16ca09f4f61f.webp","credit":"Marino Marini","license":"Image © respective rights holders · MoMA collection","url":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/81477","scope":"Representative work from the series/cycle; the timeline range covers the series, not only this image. Shown: Horse and Rider · 1942"},"imageChecked78":"2026-10-05"},{"id":"t68-1e52051620b6","title":"Statute of Westminster","lane":"history","start":1931,"end":1931,"approx":false,"note":"Recognised legislative autonomy for specified dominions; implementation differed among them.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Statute%20of%20Westminster","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["britain","shared"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-756fd68c687e","title":"The Persistence of Memory","lane":"art","start":1931,"end":1931,"approx":false,"note":"Precisely painted soft watches unsettle everyday expectations of time and material solidity.","creators":["Salvador Dalí"],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=The%20Persistence%20of%20Memory","sourceSheets":[3645],"sourceMapping":"supplemental work for a creator on the source sheet","dateType":"year","threads67":["iberia","france"],"setting67":"Cultural / geographical association; see work context","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16","image":{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?action=media&name=01fc7f4b00d1d8552112bdb3.webp","credit":"Salvador Dalí · MoMA collection reference","license":"Museum reference · reuse not cleared","url":"https://www.moma.org/explore/inside_out/2010/04/14/moma-offsite-where-did-it-go/","scope":"Exact title and artist matched to existing catalogue"},"mediaType78":"visual-artwork"},{"id":"t68-d78e7a950abc","title":"Kingdom of Saudi Arabia proclaimed","lane":"history","start":1932,"end":1932,"approx":false,"note":"Ibn Saud unified his domains under the new kingdom's name.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Kingdom%20of%20Saudi%20Arabia%20proclaimed","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-fd986043a3f8","title":"Woman with Her Throat Cut","lane":"art","start":1932,"end":1932,"approx":false,"note":"Giacometti’s Surrealist sculpture evokes violence through an ambiguous bodily form.","creators":["Alberto Giacometti"],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Woman%20with%20Her%20Throat%20Cut","sourceSheets":[3645],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["france"],"setting67":"Cultural / geographical association; see work context","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16","mediaType78":"visual-artwork","image":{"src":"/.netlify/functions/access?a