reement","lane":"history","start":1938,"end":1938,"approx":false,"note":"The Sudetenland was ceded without Czechoslovak participation in the agreement.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Munich%20Agreement","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["central","britain","france","italy"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-5754f262450d","title":"German occupation of Czech lands","lane":"history","start":1939,"end":1939,"approx":false,"note":"The occupation destroyed the remaining Czech state's independence after Munich.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=German%20occupation%20of%20Czech%20lands","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["central"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-2427b0b30a32","title":"Germany invades Poland","lane":"history","start":1939,"end":1939,"approx":false,"note":"The invasion on 1 September was followed by British and French declarations of war on 3 September.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Germany%20invades%20Poland","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["central"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-e80c3faaf9bf","title":"Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact","lane":"history","start":1939,"end":1939,"approx":false,"note":"A non-aggression agreement with secret protocols divided spheres of influence in eastern Europe.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Molotov%E2%80%93Ribbentrop%20Pact","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["central","other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-3eb1969fd236","title":"Second World War","lane":"history","start":1939,"end":1945,"approx":false,"note":"European war began with Germany's invasion of Poland; it became a global conflict with distinct theatres and end dates.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_War_II","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"period","threads67":["central","britain","france","italy","other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-2ce1426f66f1","title":"Churchill becomes prime minister","lane":"history","start":1940,"end":1940,"approx":false,"note":"He took office in May as Germany's western offensive began.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Churchill%20becomes%20prime%20minister","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["britain"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-38587dc52678","title":"De Gaulle's Appeal of 18 June","lane":"history","start":1940,"end":1940,"approx":false,"note":"The broadcast from London called for continued resistance and became a symbol of Free France.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=De%20Gaulle%27s%20Appeal%20of%2018%20June","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["france","britain"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-a02ed037f357","title":"Dunkirk evacuation","lane":"history","start":1940,"end":1940,"approx":false,"note":"Allied troops were evacuated; successful evacuation was not a battlefield victory over the German offensive.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Dunkirk%20evacuation","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["britain","france"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-6619ddcf53c7","title":"Fall of France and Vichy regime","lane":"history","start":1940,"end":1940,"approx":false,"note":"Military defeat and an armistice led to occupation and an authoritarian collaborationist regime.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Fall%20of%20France%20and%20Vichy%20regime","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["france","central"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-adb7f64030aa","title":"German invasion of Denmark and Norway","lane":"history","start":1940,"end":1940,"approx":false,"note":"The April campaign extended the war into northern Europe.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=German%20invasion%20of%20Denmark%20and%20Norway","sourceSheets":[3646],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["central","other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-1c0108f23561","title":"Abstract Expressionism emerges","lane":"art","start":1940,"end":1950,"approx":true,"note":"A diverse postwar New York movement; action painting and colour-field approaches are distinct tendencies.","creators":["Jackson Pollock","Willem de Kooning","Mark Rothko"],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Abstract%20Expressionism%20emerges","sourceSheets":[3647],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"period","threads67":["other"],"setting67":"Cultural / geographical association; see work context","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t69-0046a19bede8","title":"Action painting and colour-field painting","lane":"art","start":1940,"end":1960,"approx":true,"note":"Pollock's gestural processes differ from Rothko's broad colour fields. Both sit within a diverse Abstract Expressionist context.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Action%20painting%20and%20colour-field%20painting","sourceSheets":[],"sourceMapping":"Editorial study concept, not a photo transcription","dateType":"study window","dateQualifier":"Study period, not an event date","threads67":["other"],"setting67":"Historical / cultural study context","kind69":"concept","mediaType78":"context"},{"id":"t68-905eb7fc45c9","title":"Atlantic Charter","lane":"history","start":1941,"end":1941,"approx":false,"note":"Roosevelt and Churchill stated wartime and postwar principles before US entry into the war.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Atlantic%20Charter","sourceSheets":[3647],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["britain","other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-5ae612b6a3bf","title":"Attack on Pearl Harbor","lane":"history","start":1941,"end":1941,"approx":false,"note":"7 December in Hawaii, 8 December in Japan; the date difference in the photo reflects time zones.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Attack%20on%20Pearl%20Harbor","sourceSheets":[3647],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-3e5acaf9843d","title":"Operation Barbarossa","lane":"history","start":1941,"end":1941,"approx":false,"note":"Germany invaded the Soviet Union, breaking the 1939 non-aggression pact.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Operation%20Barbarossa","sourceSheets":[3647],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["central","other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-652ffc7e21dd","title":"Roosevelt's Four Freedoms speech","lane":"history","start":1941,"end":1941,"approx":false,"note":"Outlined freedom of speech, worship, from want and from fear.","creators":[],"reference":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?search=Roosevelt%27s%20Four%20Freedoms%20speech","sourceSheets":[3647],"sourceMapping":"item","dateType":"year","threads67":["other"],"setting67":"Historical setting","sourceBatch68":"Sheets 11–16"},{"id":"t68-1fd9e8923b25","title":"Battle of Midway","lane":"history","start":1942,"end":1942,"approx":false,"note":"A m